# Template only -- lists the variable names this stack's docker-compose.yml
# expects. Real values live in Infisical, never here and never in git.
# scripts/render-env.sh writes the actual .env next to this file on the host.
#
# This stack has no ${VAR} substitution in docker-compose.yml itself --
# both containers read their shared auth token from a Docker-secrets-style
# file (./secrets/tld_auth_token.txt), matching the central-Postgres
# pattern, rather than a plain env var. There is nothing to render into
# .env for this stack today; this file exists so the per-stack layout
# stays consistent and so future env vars (e.g. GEOIP_* if that's ever
# turned on) have somewhere obvious to go.
#
# Generate the shared token once, on the host, before first `docker compose up`:
#   mkdir -p secrets && openssl rand -hex 32 > secrets/tld_auth_token.txt
